/-!
# S9-C3h103: Cartan/action-generated coframe second-jet actual lift

This module returns to the path-first/action-first construction used before
the residual-containment detour.  On the selected bosonic positive lineage,
C3h101 supplies an actual Lorentz connection germ whose physical-time jet is
nonzero even though the initial Cartan coframe velocity is zero.  That actual
jet first generates the twelve spatial coframe accelerations

```text
source + action → actual ω germ → ω̇ᵢ
                → Cartan spatial coframe acceleration
                → quadratic local e germ
                → B := II⁺(e).
```

C3h102's scalar second jet and every other action-generated field are
retained.  The temporal coframe column remains the existing control; it is
not presented as an action output.  Simplicity and the mixed Cartan law are
proved only after the common actual configuration has been constructed.

This is a bosonic positive-lineage second-order local germ, not a generic
Einstein--Cartan flow.  With nonzero Dirac spin current, the corresponding
Cartan source must itself be generated from the representation/action before
this construction can be generalized.  No residual, quotient, preimage,
endpoint, right inverse, supplied certificate, source knob, or branch receipt
enters any constructor.
-/

namespace
  SaturationMonoid.PhysicsCore.StageNineCartanActionCoframeSecondJetLocalActualLift

open ProofFreeRicherAnholonomicSource
open PointwiseDiracSpinConnectionLift
open StageNineBlockwiseConstitutive
open StageNineCanonicalCauchyState
open StageNineEnrichedProofFreeSource
